WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.660
it does look like at least some Republican
senators are going to do the right thing and

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:10.200
they're going to vote to have key witnesses
like John Bolton testify in the Senate impeachment

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.200
trial.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.009
You'll remember we talked about it earlier,
earlier already in the context of the propaganda

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:19.410
war that is being waged at the start of Donald
Trump's Senate impeachment trial, Republicans

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:25.980
were able to get an absolutely ridiculous
decision to talk about subpoenaing witnesses

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:30.910
and documents and audio visual records after
both sides have had their 24 hours to present

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:33.750
their cases and possibly even after, uh, eat.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.820
There have been 16 hours of questions from
senators.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:41.190
This makes no sense knowing which documents
will be introduced.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:45.420
Knowing which witnesses will testify would
be hugely important to structuring your case

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.180
as would be done in any other kind of trial.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.210
But this is what Republicans were able to
pull off.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.300
Good for them, I guess.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.070
Although it's completely ridiculous.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.090
So soon this is going to become the subject
in the Senate.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:04.439
We know that you need only a simple majority
to subpoena witnesses, meaning the 45 Democrats,

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:07.700
the two independent senators who caucus with
Democrats.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.920
That's 47 and four Republicans.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.000
It seems that we have a couple of Republicans
that are going in the direction of at least

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.060
voting to subpoena John Bolton to testify.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:22.770
Uh, one of those individuals is Utah Republican
Senator Mitt Romney.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:27.889
Mitt Romney spoke to reporters and said he
has yet to decide, but he does seem to be

00:01:27.889 --> 00:01:29.799
leaning in that direction.

00:01:29.799 --> 00:01:33.200
It's increasingly apparent that it would be
important hear from John Bolton.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.609
Uh, I of course will make a final decision
on witnesses after we've heard from not only

00:01:38.609 --> 00:01:40.880
the prosecution but also the defense.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.149
But I think at this stage it's pretty fair
to say that, uh, John Bolton has a, uh, relevant,

00:01:45.149 --> 00:01:46.149
uh, testimony.

00:01:46.149 --> 00:01:51.250
I think it's increasingly likely that other
Republicans will, uh, will join those of us

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.389
who think we should hear from John Bolton.

00:01:53.389 --> 00:01:58.250
This came right after the New York times published
those excerpts from John Bolton's upcoming

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.250
book.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:04.459
His manuscript of the book were Bolton destroys
every single talking point in the defense

00:02:04.459 --> 00:02:06.380
of Donald Trump on the Ukraine issue.

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:12.370
John Bolton, very plainly and clearly saying
in his upcoming book, Trump told him withhold

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:16.780
the military aid to Ukraine until they smear
Joe Biden publicly.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:20.540
This testimony would be devastating to the
Republican narrative and to Donald Trump's

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:25.260
narrative and we're going to talk more about
what that testimony might do in a little bit.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:30.000
We also heard from Senator Susan Collins,
Susan Collins, Republican Senator from Maine.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.459
She often is very concerned about something,
but then ends up voting with Republicans.

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:39.269
She put out a statement where she said from
the beginning, I've said that in fairness

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:43.349
to both parties, the decision on whether or
not to call witnesses should be made after

00:02:43.349 --> 00:02:47.430
both the house managers and the president's
attorneys have had the opportunity to present

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:48.430
their cases.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:49.430
She's wrong about that.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:53.709
The decision should be made earlier, but okay,
this is her position going on to say, I've

00:02:53.709 --> 00:02:58.859
always said that I was likely to vote to call
witnesses just as I did in the 1999 Clinton

00:02:58.859 --> 00:02:59.859
trial.

00:02:59.859 --> 00:03:03.730
The reports about John Bolton's book strengthen
the case for witnesses and have prompted a

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.720
number of conversations among my colleagues.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:11.270
So that's potentially two Republicans who
will join the Democrats and independents that

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:13.219
would make 49 votes.

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:16.590
You still need two more to get to the 51 that
are needed.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:22.000
But increasingly there are rumblings that
there will be four, at least four Republicans

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.109
who vote to subpoena John Bolton.

00:03:24.109 --> 00:03:29.750
Now, even if John Bolton shows up, you aren't
going to get a conviction of Donald Trump,

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:30.819
but that's not relevant.

00:03:30.819 --> 00:03:35.780
Now, we knew that going in and exposing what
John Bolton has to say to the widest possible

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:41.249
audience, once again, confirming the brazen
nature of Donald Trump's lies would be a very

00:03:41.249 --> 00:03:42.249
good thing.

00:03:42.249 --> 00:03:48.999
There's always a risk that Republican senators
will say, I lean towards testifying or whatever,

00:03:48.999 --> 00:03:50.689
and then they don't actually vote for it.

00:03:50.689 --> 00:03:53.109
In the end, Susan Collins has done that many
times.

00:03:53.109 --> 00:03:56.469
Go back to the cabinet hearings until they
actually vote.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.709
I will assume nothing of them.

00:03:58.709 --> 00:04:02.249
Um, but it looks like this may actually become
a reality.

00:04:02.249 --> 00:04:06.920
John Bolton's testimony, Romney politically
would suffer no consequences from his vote.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:11.829
By the way, Mitt Romney could get reelected
indefinitely in Utah as long as he wants,

00:04:11.829 --> 00:04:12.829
no matter what he does.

00:04:12.829 --> 00:04:15.079
As many of you know, Utah has a large Mormon
population.

00:04:15.079 --> 00:04:16.139
Mitt Romney is Mormon.

00:04:16.139 --> 00:04:18.220
Utah is also very conservative.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:22.470
Mitt Romney has that seat for essentially
as long as he wants it.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:26.480
Hopefully he's not just saying he'd consider
voting that way.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.970
And actually we'll, we've, we've been disillusioned
before.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:34.060
We've seen Mitt Romney and Susan Collins,
sometimes Lisa Murkowski, they pretend to

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:35.060
have a spine.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.320
They pretend to have morals.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.440
They say they're very worried and then they
just vote with Republicans.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.980
So we'll believe it if and when we see it,
it will do nothing to secure votes for the

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:48.660
conviction of Donald Trump from Republicans.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:51.150
Remember that I just don't trust them.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:55.610
And anything that depends on a few Republicans
acting appropriately, we've learned over the

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:56.730
last 20 years.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.750
It's just not something we can count on in
American politics.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:05.290
But let's now get to the effect of the Bolton
testimony because Republicans are panicking

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:09.060
about what that possible testimony could mean.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:10.110
And could cause.

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:42.420
So let's

00:05:42.420 --> 00:06:38.240
talk about

00:06:38.240 --> 00:07:09.830
that next.

